{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.ConjRhoKPairGenCanonicalForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.ConjRhoKPairGenCanonicalForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.PairGenCanonical.content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.PairGenCanonical.content","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form.lean#L102-L102","doc":"Uniform sub-percent recovery of every atomic braid's measured pair-gen\nmass `physMass K` by one concrete `T_3` quantum-dilogarithm functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.PairGenCanonical.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.PairGenCanonical.mk","kind":"ctor","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.PairGenCanonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.PairGenCanonical","kind":"class","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form.lean#L74-L105","doc":"**Conjecture (AGENTS.md §3b class axiomatisation, content-bearing).**\nThere is a single pair-gen functional of the six-term `T_3`\nKashaev-limit form `-z² · Li₂^q(-|V_i V_j|)` — with `Li₂^q = qDilog q`\nthe quantum dilogarithm and `z` the categorical scale — whose pairwise\nsum over every atomic braid's Wedderburn-traced per-generator volumes\nrecovers that braid's measured pair-gen mass to sub-percent accuracy.\n\nThe naive log-additive `f` is refuted empirically\n(`rho-k-pair-gen-extension.witness.json`); the conjectured `T_3` form is\nbelieved correct but its Kashaev-limit derivation is open. The\nconjecture is axiomatised here as a `Prop` class — downstream blocks\ncarry it as an explicit `[PairGenCanonical]` hypothesis per §3b-cond.\n\n**Content-bearing (fixes the prior vacuous field).** The previous field\n`∀ M ≥ 0, ∃ M_rec, |M_rec − M| ≤ M/100` was trivially provable\n(`M_rec := M`), asserting nothing. Here the recovered value is\n`pairSum (kashaevT3 (qDilog q) z) K.vols` — a *fixed function of the\nbraid's Markov data* — and the target `physMass K` is a *function* of the\nsame braid, so the field is neither trivially provable (the recovered\nvalue cannot copy the target) nor trivially refutable (one braid has one\nmeasured mass). An instance genuinely requires exhibiting a single\nsubstrate `q` and scale `z` for which the concrete quantum-dilogarithm\nfunctional meets the sub-percent bound UNIFORMLY across all atomic braids\n— the open Kashaev-limit derivation. **No instance is provided** (the\nhonest open state). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form","label":"conj:rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.kashaevT3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.kashaevT3","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form.lean#L68-L72","doc":"The six-term theorem's `T_3` Kashaev-limit pair-gen functional\n`f(x, y) = -z² · Li₂^q(-|x·y|)`, assembled from the quantum-dilogarithm\nregulator `Li2q` and the categorical scale `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.pairSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.pairSum","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form.lean#L62-L66","doc":"Pairwise sum `Σ_{i<j} f (vᵢ) (vⱼ)` of a binary functional over a list of\nper-generator volumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.physMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.physMass","kind":"opaque","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form.lean#L50-L60","doc":"The measured (CODATA) pair-gen mass contribution `ρ_K^{pair-gen}` of an\natomic braid — an **external empirical datum**, hence an opaque function\nof the braid's Markov data (a *function*, so the same braid has a single\nmeasured mass; this is what keeps the recovery claim below refutation-\nfree rather than trivially false). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.AtomicBraid.vols","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.AtomicBraid.vols","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Wedderburn-traced per-generator volumes `|V̂_i|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.AtomicBraid.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.AtomicBraid.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.AtomicBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.AtomicBraid","kind":"structure","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form.lean#L43-L48","doc":"Markov datum for one atomic braid: the Wedderburn-traced per-generator\nvolumes `|V̂_i|` (real numbers, read off the Markov trace of the\nstandard-representation transfer matrices). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.qDilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKPairGenCanonicalForm.qDilog","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-rho-k-pair-gen-canonical-form.lean#L35-L41","doc":"The **quantum dilogarithm** `Li₂^q` as a concrete real function — the\nFaddeev–Kashaev series `Li₂^q(x) = Σ_{n≥1} xⁿ / (n · (1 − qⁿ))`\n(the `def:q-dilogarithm` regulator, evaluated over `ℝ`). Noncomputable\n(an infinite sum); `tsum` is total, so this is well-defined as a term\neven where the series fails to converge. ","signatureChunk":0}]}